TITLE:: PartCommand
SUMMARY:: Command that sets the part on selected piano-roll notes.
CATEGORIES:: Commands
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/Parameter, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollNote, Classes/SetCommand

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::PartCommand:: is a LINK::Classes/Command:: named CODE::part:: that sets the part of each selected LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote::. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: supplies the notes through LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt#-ambientParameters:: as CODE::selectedNotes::. The record-context number keys CODE::1:: to CODE::9:: call this command with one value.

CODE::values:: is a space-separated list of LINK::Classes/Integer::s from CODE::1:: to CODE::9::. Notes are ordered by CODE::startTime:: only. Notes that share a start time take the same array value; the list wraps and advances only when start time changes. A single value, such as CODE::2::, therefore sets every selected note to that part. Each note that responds to CODE::assignPart:: stores the part and asks the roll to paint it. A note that does not, such as a LINK::Classes/DrumStep::, is left unchanged, and this command is not offered on the drum programmer.

The roll paints part 1 with LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour1::, part 2 with LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour2::, part 3 with LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour3::, part 4 with LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour4::, and part 5 with LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour5::. Part 6 uses colour1 again. Part 9 uses colour4. LINK::Classes/SetCommand:: on the piano roll includes this command, so CODE::set key part:: borrows the same 1–9 constraint.

Example: four notes at beats CODE::0, 1, 1, 2:: with CODE::part values 1 9:: become parts CODE::1, 9, 9, 1::.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::PartCommand::. Takes no arguments; parts are applied by LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::PartCommand:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: execute
Applies wrapped part numbers to CODE::\selectedNotes:: grouped by start time.

ARGUMENT:: args
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\selectedNotes:: (an LINK::Classes/Array:: of notes that respond to CODE::assignPart::) and CODE::\values:: (a non-empty LINK::Classes/Array:: of LINK::Classes/Integer::s from CODE::1:: to CODE::9::).
